<section class="panel">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="eyebrow">Route 3 &middot; from scratch</div>
		<h1>Install postmarketOS yourself</h1>
		<p class="lede">For a phone that has never run Linux, or if you want to build
		your own system instead of flashing mine. The POCO X3 NFC has no port of its
		own: it uses the generic <code>qcom-sm7150</code>, which needs U-Boot and
		systemd.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>01</span><h2>Unlock the bootloader</h2></div>
		<p>Xiaomi's own procedure, with its waiting period. Everything is wiped.</p>

		<div class="h" style="margin-top:34px"><span>02</span><h2>U-Boot, matched to your panel</h2></div>
		<p><b>Tianma or Huaxing.</b> Get it wrong and the screen stays black &mdash;
		the phone is fine, it just draws nothing. Check which one you have before
		flashing.</p>
		<div class="sh">
			<div class="bar"><i></i><span>ON YOUR PC</span></div>
			<pre><i># releases: github.com/sm7150-mainline/u-boot</i>
fastboot erase dtbo
fastboot flash boot u-boot-sm7150-xiaomi-surya-tianma.img</pre>
		</div>
		<p>This is the only thing that ever goes to <code>boot</code>. The kernel
		lives inside the system image on <code>userdata</code>.</p>

		<div class="h" style="margin-top:34px"><span>03</span><h2>Build a system with pmbootstrap</h2></div>
		<div class="sh">
			<div class="bar"><i></i><span>ON YOUR PC</span></div>
			<pre>pmbootstrap init            <i># device: qcom-sm7150, UI: plasma-mobile</i>
pmbootstrap config service_manager systemd   <b># with OpenRC the image comes out broken</b>
pmbootstrap install
pmbootstrap flasher flash_rootfs             <b># goes to userdata</b></pre>
		</div>
		<p>That gives you a stock postmarketOS: no working cameras, no in-call voice,
		muted speakers, locked GPS. Which is what the next step is for.</p>

		<div class="h" style="margin-top:34px"><span>04</span><h2>Add this repository</h2></div>
		<p>Three commands, and the phone becomes the one described on the front page.</p>
		<p><a class="btn" href="install-repo.html">Route 2 &rarr;</a></p>
